cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Security Audit of the National Network Identity Authentication Android Client
  (cn.cyberIdentity.certification v1.2.40): Cryptography Use and
  Security-Engineering Deficiencies
message: >-
  If you use this audit report, please cite it as below and state the verified
  APK fingerprint (SHA-256 1b6368cf320d68b7aa6eab67c458cf1f5849ed9da079f1741d8a41f6553dfedf).
type: report
authors:
  - name: Math Fournity
    email: math-fournity@proton.me
  - name: GLM-5.3
repository-code: "https://github.com/math-fournity/cn.cyberIdentity.certification"
abstract: >-
  Independent static security audit of China's official National Network Identity
  Authentication Android client. Findings: hardcoded plaintext SM4 keys (including
  a self-described test key) and ECB-mode primitives in the CloudWalk (688327)
  face-liveness SDK shipped inside the app; an unstripped debug-log surface
  including a key-seed print statement; packer coverage of only 33% leaving all
  security-relevant configuration outside the encrypted region. All claims are
  tied to binary addresses and reproducible with public tooling.
keywords:
  - security audit
  - Android
  - SM4
  - ECB mode
  - hardcoded key
  - CTID
  - network identity authentication
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-10-24"
version: "1.1"
language: zh
